1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,500
Uncle, I'm home on leave!

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:04,900
Oh, Private First Class! Let me tell you, back in my day…

3
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:07,300
Whatever the seniors make us do… it's all bullying…

4
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:12,167
Hey, rookie! Fold my socks. It's for your training~

5
00:00:12,167 --> 00:00:14,933
Uncle, that's against regulations now.

6
00:00:14,933 --> 00:00:15,533
…Huh?

7
00:00:15,533 --> 00:00:20,900
As a private: bullying. As a sergeant: training. Double standard, number one.

8
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:23,433
I'm… Modapman.

9
00:00:25,433 --> 00:00:30,233
Case summary. Saturday night, Korean BBQ. Celebrating a nephew's leave.

10
00:00:30,233 --> 00:00:31,700
Dad, what's "jjam"?

11
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:35,000
How many army meals you've eaten. The more, the stronger.

12
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,700
Just four rounds. Round one: work detail.

13
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:42,133
We're digging in the blazing sun, and the sergeant just "supervises" from the shade…

14
00:00:42,133 --> 00:00:44,433
Hey, nice shovel angle there~

15
00:00:44,433 --> 00:00:46,533
How is that work?!

16
00:00:46,533 --> 00:00:50,600
I lead with experience~ So what.

17
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:51,900
So you were in the shade too?

18
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:57,967
They rest: slacking. I rest: leadership. Double standard, number two.

19
00:00:57,967 --> 00:01:01,033
When others rest, they're lazy. When I rest, I have my reasons.

20
00:01:01,033 --> 00:01:02,933
It's called the actor-observer bias.

21
00:01:02,933 --> 00:01:04,833
Round two: cleaning.

22
00:01:04,833 --> 00:01:06,900
Everything's spotless, even the window frames!

23
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:08,967
Dust. Again.

24
00:01:08,967 --> 00:01:11,267
Dust. Again~

25
00:01:11,267 --> 00:01:14,500
Sergeant, your locker… there's ramen soup…

26
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:17,567
That's not dirt. That's a memory.

27
00:01:17,567 --> 00:01:23,367
Their dust: a violation. My dust: a memory. Double standard, number three.

28
00:01:23,367 --> 00:01:27,900
Seeing others' flaws but not your own — that's the bias blind spot.

29
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:28,833
…The meat's burning. Flip it.

30
00:01:28,833 --> 00:01:30,867
Round three: leave.

31
00:01:30,867 --> 00:01:34,867
The seniors take all the good dates, and I get the leftovers…

32
00:01:34,867 --> 00:01:38,267
Leave goes by seniority. Obviously.

33
00:01:38,267 --> 00:01:41,267
Um… I'd like to request leave next month…

34
00:01:41,267 --> 00:01:41,833
Already?!

35
00:01:41,833 --> 00:01:47,000
They go: already? I go: obviously. Double standard, number four.

36
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,100
Uncle, leave isn't about seniority. It's guaranteed by law.

37
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:53,833
"Service members are guaranteed leave, passes, and overnights."

38
00:01:53,833 --> 00:01:54,600
That's in the LAW?!

39
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:57,367
Final round four: the march.

40
00:01:57,367 --> 00:02:00,600
Carrying the seniors' packs too… isn't this bullying…

41
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:08,000
I'm 30 days from discharge. Making a civilian carry stuff? Now THAT'S illegal!

42
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,100
Isn't this bullying…

43
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:12,867
Kids these days, so mouthy~

44
00:02:12,867 --> 00:02:18,800
When I say it: speaking up. When they say it: talking back. Double standard, number five.

45
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:21,500
Uncle, 30 days left is still a soldier.

46
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:26,400
When you're not hurting, you underestimate someone else's pain. The empathy gap.

47
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:29,233
Bonus round. Rapid-fire double standards!

48
00:02:29,233 --> 00:02:31,600
They hog the remote: dictatorship. I do: seniority!

49
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:33,933
They shower first: cutting in line. I do: rank!

50
00:02:33,933 --> 00:02:36,267
They take two pieces: greedy. I do: fitness management!

51
00:02:36,267 --> 00:02:40,467
Double standard: six, seven, eight!

52
00:02:40,467 --> 00:02:44,533
Still, back in my day there was romance. The army's easy these days, right?

53
00:02:44,533 --> 00:02:47,033
It's not easy. There's just nobody bossing you around.

54
00:02:47,033 --> 00:02:50,533
A lot of units room you with your own intake, and after hours we can use our phones.

55
00:02:50,533 --> 00:02:52,933
…Then who bosses the rookie around?

56
00:02:52,933 --> 00:02:53,833
Nobody.

57
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:56,267
Dad, was it hard being a private?

58
00:02:56,267 --> 00:02:57,867
Yeah. Really hard.

59
00:02:57,867 --> 00:03:02,100
Then it must be hard for him now too. You grill today, Dad.

60
00:03:02,100 --> 00:03:05,200
…Okay. Tonight, your uncle grills.

61
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:07,467
Alright, rookie! Wrap one up and feed it to Daddy~

62
00:03:07,467 --> 00:03:09,900
Uncle, that's against regulations now.

63
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:12,100
This is a BBQ restaurant!

64
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:14,900
Honey, you were discharged twenty years ago.

65
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:20,400
They give orders: bullying. I give orders: family love. Double standard, number nine.

66
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:25,067
The tongs changed hands, but the seniority stayed. Just a wrong answer.

67
00:03:25,067 --> 00:03:26,767
…Classic Modapman.
